# Observability and security

## Observability

- OTEL spans: HTTP, Wolverine, EF, RabbitMQ, Python, tools, models.
- W3C trace context on HTTP + CloudEvents.
- Structured logs: service, env, traceId, spanId, correlationId, operationId, messageId, errorCode.
- Metrics: latency/error, queue depth/age, outbox age, AI duration/tokens/cost, time-in-state.
- Audit events = immutable business/security ledger (not logs).
- Never log source bodies, full prompts, tokens, cookies, secrets, or PII by default.

## Security

- Cookie auth + antiforgery; MFA for Admin.
- Named capability policies; least privilege.
- Ingest: allow schemes; DNS safe; deny private/metadata; revalidate redirects; size/type limits.
- Webhook signature verify when available; always reconcile.
- AI tools allowlisted; no general shell/DB/arbitrary network.
- Human approval required for claims, final content, publication confirm.
